00:42:23.230 --> 00:42:28.850
Well, in the break room, Pam is eating yogurt when Erin enters to ask her to look over an itinerary.
在休息室里，帕姆正在吃酸奶，这时艾琳进来请她帮忙看一份行程表。

886
00:42:29.650 --> 00:42:30.410
That's right.
没错。

887
00:42:30.410 --> 00:42:38.330
We had a fan catch from Kelsey in Kentucky who said, when Phyllis, Pam, and Erin are in the break room looking at the itinerary,
我们收到了一位来自肯塔基州的粉丝凯尔西的反馈，她说，当菲利斯、帕姆和艾琳在休息室看行程表时，

888
00:42:38.510 --> 00:42:42.210
it's very obvious again how much purple is in the wardrobe design.
很明显，服装设计里又用了大量的紫色。

889
00:42:42.210 --> 00:42:43.110
Oh, I noticed.
哦，我注意到了。

890
00:42:43.390 --> 00:42:48.530
And later in the bullpen, you'll notice Angela Martin also has a purple lilac cardigan.
后来在办公区，你会发现安吉拉·马丁也穿了一件紫丁香色的开衫。

891
00:42:48.670 --> 00:42:49.510
It was a purple day.
那真是个“紫色日”。

892
00:42:49.750 --> 00:42:52.150
You and Kelsey are sharing a brain today.
你和凯尔西今天真是心有灵犀。

893
00:42:52.310 --> 00:42:52.670
We are.
确实。

894
00:42:52.670 --> 00:42:58.870
Well, this itinerary has one very interesting line item.
这份行程表里有一项非常有趣的条目。

895
00:42:59.330 --> 00:43:03.370
Pam is surprised to learn that the Michael Scott Foundation is still in existence.
帕姆惊讶地发现“迈克尔·斯科特基金会”竟然还存在。

896
00:43:03.870 --> 00:43:06.370
And Phyllis says, what's Scott's tots?
菲利斯问，“斯科特的学童”是什么？

897
00:43:06.370 --> 00:43:11.070
And Stanley starts laughing and says, has it really been 10 years?
斯坦利开始大笑，说，真的已经十年了吗？

898
00:43:11.370 --> 00:43:13.270
I mean, Stanley isn't just laughing.
我的意思是，斯坦利不仅仅是在笑。

899
00:43:13.570 --> 00:43:19.750
It is a laugh that comes, like, from a deep place of like, oh, this guy is screwed.
那笑声仿佛来自内心深处，带着一种“哦，这家伙死定了”的感觉。

900
00:43:19.930 --> 00:43:22.370
And I am thrilled to watch it happen.
而且我很兴奋能看到这一幕发生。

901
00:43:22.930 --> 00:43:26.150
Well, Stanley's going to hold up a newspaper.
嗯，斯坦利要举起一份报纸。

902
00:43:26.450 --> 00:43:31.570
The headline reads, local businessman pledges college tuition to third graders.
头条写着：当地商人承诺资助三年级学生大学学费。

903
00:43:32.730 --> 00:43:35.330
We kind of talked about this with BJ a little bit.
我们之前和BJ稍微聊过这个。

904
00:43:35.330 --> 00:43:39.610
And we got a fan mail flurry about this newspaper article that Stanley's holding up.
关于斯坦利举着的那份报纸，我们收到了大量的粉丝来信。

905
00:43:40.890 --> 00:43:43.350
Because it looks like the real Scranton Times.
因为它看起来就像真的《斯克兰顿时报》一样。

906
00:43:43.670 --> 00:43:44.590
It really does.
确实很像。

907
00:43:44.890 --> 00:43:47.190
This is fakie filet, but it's done amazingly.
这是伪造的，但做得非常棒。

908
00:43:47.530 --> 00:43:51.210
It is actually a real Scranton Times newspaper.
它实际上就是一份真正的《斯克兰顿时报》。

909
00:43:52.110 --> 00:43:55.350
Randy Cordray explained how we made this amazing prop.
兰迪·科德雷解释了我们是如何制作这个惊人道具的。

910
00:43:55.770 --> 00:44:00.350
So first, they hired a group of kids to take a picture with Michael Scott at school.
首先，他们雇了一群孩子在学校和迈克尔·斯科特合影。

911
00:44:00.350 --> 00:44:05.990
And Kim Ferry even styled Steve's hair in a retro Caesar-style hairdo.
金·费里甚至给史蒂夫设计了一个复古的凯撒式发型。

912
00:44:06.130 --> 00:44:10.110
You know that one that was made popular by George Clooney in the early years of ER?
你知道那种乔治·克鲁尼在《急诊室的故事》早期带火的发型吗？

913
00:44:10.330 --> 00:44:11.170
Oh, yes.
噢，知道。

914
00:44:11.230 --> 00:44:11.510
Yes.
是的。

915
00:44:11.690 --> 00:44:14.150
I mean, that's how detailed they were about this photo.
我是说，他们对这张照片的细节要求有多高。

916
00:44:14.290 --> 00:44:15.930
They think Michael Scott would be into this hairdo.
他们认为迈克尔·斯科特会喜欢这种发型。

917
00:44:15.930 --> 00:44:23.270
So then Phil Shea contacted the Scranton Times and asked for a copy of their newspaper from 10 years ago.
于是菲尔·谢联系了《斯克兰顿时报》，索要了他们十年前的一份报纸。

918
00:44:24.230 --> 00:44:26.410
And when he was looking through it, he said,
当他翻看报纸时，他说，

919
00:44:26.690 --> 00:44:31.450
Do you think you would be willing to reproduce the local page?
你们愿意重新排版一下本地新闻版面吗？

920
00:44:31.450 --> 00:44:39.950
So not the front page, but the local page with a different feature story at the bottom of the page so that we can use it on our show.
不是头版，而是本地新闻版，在页面底部放上一篇不同的专题报道，这样我们就能在剧里使用了。

921
00:44:40.790 --> 00:44:41.230
Wow.
哇。

922
00:44:41.850 --> 00:44:48.130
So the writers wrote a fake article, and Randy Shemansky, who worked at the Times, put it all together.
编剧们写了一篇假文章，在《时报》工作的兰迪·谢曼斯基把它整合在了一起。

923
00:44:48.130 --> 00:44:52.890
He put his name as the writer in the byline and printed it for us.
他把自己的名字写在署名栏里，并为我们印刷了出来。

924
00:44:53.330 --> 00:44:54.290
Nice, Randy.
干得好，兰迪。

925
00:44:54.510 --> 00:44:55.190
Thank you.
谢谢。

926
00:44:55.730 --> 00:44:57.470
Well, that's why it looks so real.
难怪它看起来那么真实。

927
00:44:57.690 --> 00:44:57.930
Yeah.
是啊。

928
00:44:58.390 --> 00:45:03.370
Well, there's photos of it online, and there's also some on Office Tally, and I'll put some of those in our stories.
网上有它的照片，Office Tally上也有一些，我会把它们放到我们的故事里。

929
00:45:03.370 --> 00:45:10.930
Yes, the entire text of the article is on officetally.com, and I thought I would read one of my favorite passages.
是的，文章全文都在officetally.com上，我想读一下我最喜欢的一段。

930
00:45:10.950 --> 00:45:17.450
The whole thing is worth a read, but this one really goes with the episode.
整篇文章都值得一读，但这一段真的非常契合这集内容。

931
00:45:17.910 --> 00:45:18.770
It says,
上面写着，

932
00:45:42.650 --> 00:45:43.630
That's in the article.
那是文章里的内容。

933
00:45:43.830 --> 00:45:44.870
It's very on theme.
非常切题。

934
00:45:44.870 --> 00:45:45.630
I know.
我知道。

935
00:45:45.910 --> 00:45:49.230
Well, Jenna, I have a little section I'm calling According to the Internet.
珍娜，我有一个小栏目，我叫它“据互联网所知”。

936
00:45:49.930 --> 00:45:50.450
Oh.
噢。

937
00:45:50.710 --> 00:45:50.990
Yeah.
是啊。

938
00:45:51.170 --> 00:45:54.570
When you type in Scott's Tots, lots of stuff comes up.
当你输入“斯科特的托特们”时，会出现很多东西。

939
00:45:54.690 --> 00:45:56.130
I'm going to share three with you.
我要和你分享三个。

940
00:45:56.650 --> 00:46:00.690
The first one is, according to the Internet, you might ask yourself,
第一个是，据互联网所知，你可能会问自己，

941
00:46:00.830 --> 00:46:04.010
how much money would Michael have to pay for all of their tuition?
迈克尔得为他们所有人的学费支付多少钱？

942
00:46:04.450 --> 00:46:04.830
Oh.
噢。

943
00:46:04.830 --> 00:46:14.850
Assuming all 15 of Scott's Tots attended a four-year private university, Michael would probably have to pay something around $1.9 million.
假设所有15个“斯科特的托特们”都上了四年制私立大学，迈克尔可能需要支付大约190万美元。

944
00:46:15.810 --> 00:46:16.450
Wow.
哇。

945
00:46:17.190 --> 00:46:17.690
Yeah.
是啊。

946
00:46:18.010 --> 00:46:25.270
So when he made this promise 10 years ago, he believed he would have so much money that he'd have like an extra $2 million.
所以当他在十年前做出这个承诺时，他以为自己会有很多钱，多到能有200万美元的闲钱。

947
00:46:25.450 --> 00:46:25.910
That's right.
没错。

948
00:46:26.590 --> 00:46:34.850
Number two, if you go to Oklahoma State University in Stillwater, Oklahoma, you can join a student club called Scott's Tots.
第二点，如果你去俄克拉荷马州斯蒂尔沃特的俄克拉荷马州立大学，你可以加入一个叫“斯科特的托特们”的学生社团。

949
00:46:35.150 --> 00:46:36.630
What does Scott's Tots do?
“斯科特的托特们”是做什么的？

950
00:46:36.630 --> 00:46:42.670
According to the online newspaper of the school, The O'Colley, staff reporter Jake Sellers wrote,
根据该校的在线校报《The O'Colley》，特约记者杰克·塞勒斯写道，

951
00:46:43.170 --> 00:46:49.150
members of the Scott's Tots Club meet weekly to stream and test their knowledge on NBC's The Office.
“斯科特的小孩”俱乐部成员每周聚会，一起观看并测试他们对NBC剧集《办公室》的了解程度。

952
00:46:49.450 --> 00:46:54.490
This semester, the club started fresh, mostly meeting in classroom building on Wednesdays.
这个学期，俱乐部重新开始活动，大多在周三于教学楼聚会。

953
00:46:54.590 --> 00:46:55.790
And it goes on to say,
文中接着写道，

954
00:46:56.350 --> 00:47:01.690
although this club may be a time for some students to watch a show, for some it is a time to connect.
虽然这个俱乐部对一些学生来说只是看剧的时间，但对另一些人来说，这是建立联系的契机。

955
00:47:02.370 --> 00:47:06.730
Haley McCauley, senior business manager, is the secretary of Scott's Tots.
海莉·麦考利，大四商科生，是“斯科特的小孩”俱乐部的秘书。

956
00:47:07.150 --> 00:47:13.250
McCauley joined in the fall of her freshman year, and she says they have trivia nights with prizes for the winners.
麦考利在大一秋季学期加入了俱乐部，她说他们会举办知识竞赛，并为获胜者提供奖品。

957
00:47:13.430 --> 00:47:16.170
And quote, she says, it's a really fun club.
引用她的话说，这是一个非常有趣的俱乐部。

958
00:47:16.650 --> 00:47:16.970
Hmm.
嗯。

959
00:47:17.390 --> 00:47:20.510
The article also included a flyer they had made for their club.
文章还附上了他们为俱乐部制作的传单。

960
00:47:20.710 --> 00:47:21.810
I'm going to put it in our stories.
我会把它发到我们的快拍里。

961
00:47:22.330 --> 00:47:23.330
Oh, I love it.
噢，我太喜欢了。

962
00:47:23.350 --> 00:47:25.450
It's got a gym face on it and a dundee.
上面有吉姆的脸，还有邓迪奖杯。

963
00:47:25.770 --> 00:47:27.410
Yeah, and the stapler and the jello.
没错，还有订书机和果冻。

964
00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:31.030
It says it has their campus link, and this is what it says.
上面写着他们的校园链接，内容是这样的。

965
00:47:31.030 --> 00:47:33.990
We watch The Office show and have trivia nights once a month.
我们观看《办公室》，每月举办一次知识竞赛。

966
00:47:34.130 --> 00:47:35.530
We have snacks!
我们还有零食！

967
00:47:36.690 --> 00:47:38.310
Well, you and I are going.
好吧，你和我都要去。

968
00:47:38.490 --> 00:47:38.950
I know.
我知道。

969
00:47:39.150 --> 00:47:40.870
And then it says where you can join to be a member.
然后上面写了加入成为会员的方式。

970
00:47:41.210 --> 00:47:45.950
And according to the internet number three, I found a ton, like too many to list,
根据互联网上的第三条信息，我发现了一大堆，多到数不过来，

971
00:47:46.610 --> 00:47:51.270
youth soccer teams named Scott's Tots all across the United States.
全美各地都有叫“斯科特的小孩”的青少年足球队。

972
00:47:51.570 --> 00:47:52.050
Wow.
哇。

973
00:47:52.350 --> 00:47:52.610
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

974
00:47:52.730 --> 00:47:57.050
You can go cheer on Scott's Tots at almost any soccer field on a Saturday in America.
在美国的周六，你几乎可以在任何足球场为“斯科特的小孩”加油助威。

975
00:47:57.290 --> 00:47:59.630
So that's some stuff I found on the internet.
这就是我在网上发现的一些东西。

976
00:47:59.630 --> 00:48:05.270
But we should go back to the break room because Pam has a very different reaction than Stanley
但我们应该回到休息室，因为帕姆对这个消息的反应

977
00:48:05.270 --> 00:48:06.190
to this information.
和斯坦利截然不同。

978
00:48:06.570 --> 00:48:10.750
I mean, Pam uses the word terrible like five times.
我是说，帕姆用了大概五次“太糟糕了”这个词。

979
00:48:10.930 --> 00:48:11.090
Yeah.
没错。

980
00:48:11.670 --> 00:48:14.230
She feels like she's not getting through to Michael.
她觉得她无法说服迈克尔。

981
00:48:14.410 --> 00:48:17.190
She's like, why would you promise something like that?
她就像是在说，你为什么要承诺那种事？

982
00:48:17.350 --> 00:48:19.530
This is a terrible thing, Michael.
这太糟糕了，迈克尔。

983
00:48:19.770 --> 00:48:20.950
This is terrible.
这太糟糕了。

984
00:48:21.290 --> 00:48:22.430
It's just terrible.
简直太糟糕了。

985
00:48:22.430 --> 00:48:25.010
And she's like, you have to go tell them now.
她还说，你现在必须去告诉他们。

986
00:48:25.810 --> 00:48:31.690
Did you see the article, Angela, where it sort of broke down there are two reactions
安吉拉，你看到那篇文章了吗？它分析了观众对这一集

987
00:48:31.690 --> 00:48:33.370
to this episode from viewers.
有两种反应。

988
00:48:33.370 --> 00:48:36.210
You're either a Stanley or a Pam.
你要么是斯坦利，要么是帕姆。

989
00:48:36.470 --> 00:48:41.490
Like it was saying, you're either a person who laughs through tragedy.
文章说，你要么是一个在悲剧中也能笑出来的人。

990
00:48:41.770 --> 00:48:42.050
Yeah.
没错。

991
00:48:42.050 --> 00:48:44.830
You know, you're that person at the funeral who gets the giggles.
你知道，就是那种在葬礼上会忍不住偷笑的人。

992
00:48:45.090 --> 00:48:45.270
Right.
对。

993
00:48:45.470 --> 00:48:48.390
Or you have no sense of humor about it.
或者你对这种事完全没有幽默感。

994
00:48:48.710 --> 00:48:53.130
They were sort of saying like, if you're a Pam, you probably can't watch this episode.
他们大概是说，如果你是帕姆那种人，你可能没法看这一集。

995
00:48:53.330 --> 00:48:53.670
Right.
没错。

996
00:48:53.890 --> 00:48:55.930
It's a really interesting article, actually.
说实话，那是一篇非常有趣的文章。

997
00:48:56.110 --> 00:48:57.370
It's on decider.com.
发表在decider.com上。

998
00:48:57.790 --> 00:49:00.090
And I don't know which one I am.
我不知道我属于哪一种。

999
00:49:00.170 --> 00:49:02.010
I mean, I have a visceral reaction.
我是说，我有种发自内心的反应。

1000
00:49:02.170 --> 00:49:03.610
Like I feel so bad for these kids.
我真的为这些孩子们感到难过。

1001
00:49:03.790 --> 00:49:07.610
And I also see Stanley finally getting to see Michael get his comeuppance.
而且我也看到斯坦利终于看到迈克尔得到了应有的报应。

1002
00:49:08.130 --> 00:49:08.510
Yes.
是的。

1003
00:49:09.250 --> 00:49:11.230
I don't know which one I am either.
我也不知道我是哪一种。

1004
00:49:11.230 --> 00:49:12.630
I enjoyed this episode.
我很喜欢这一集。

1005
00:49:12.630 --> 00:49:14.830
So I guess I must be a little Stanley.
所以我猜我一定有点像斯坦利。

1006
00:49:15.670 --> 00:49:16.930
Maybe we're a combo.
也许我们是两者的结合体。

1007
00:49:17.410 --> 00:49:18.930
I don't know who that would be.
我不知道那会是谁。

1008
00:49:19.070 --> 00:49:20.070
Are you an Aaron then?
那你是个亚伦吗？

1009
00:49:20.790 --> 00:49:22.450
Aaron seems horrified.
亚伦看起来很震惊。

1010
00:49:22.710 --> 00:49:27.810
And yet also, she still finds a positive spin at the end.
然而，她最后还是找到了积极的一面。

1011
00:49:28.250 --> 00:49:29.490
Yeah, maybe we're Aaron.
是啊，也许我们是亚伦。

1012
00:49:29.910 --> 00:49:34.890
The article said about people who are Stanleys, and I thought this was worded really well.
文章里提到了那些像斯坦利一样的人，我觉得措辞非常到位。

1013
00:49:35.070 --> 00:49:36.410
They're not heartless.
他们并非铁石心肠。

1014
00:49:36.410 --> 00:49:39.510
They're almost shocked to the point of hilarity.
他们几乎震惊到想笑的地步。

1015
00:49:39.810 --> 00:49:40.270
Right.
没错。

1016
00:49:40.570 --> 00:49:44.830
When something is so insanely absurd to you that someone could do that, that you're like, what?
当某件事荒谬到让你觉得怎么会有人做出这种事，你会想，什么鬼？

1017
00:49:45.710 --> 00:49:47.130
That's their coping mechanism.
那是他们的应对机制。

1018
00:49:47.310 --> 00:49:47.510
Yeah.
是的。

1019
00:49:47.850 --> 00:49:48.130
Right.
没错。

1020
00:49:48.750 --> 00:49:51.050
Whereas Pam, it's just all just torturous.
而对帕姆来说，这一切简直是折磨。

1021
00:49:51.750 --> 00:49:52.310
Yeah.
是啊。

1022
00:49:53.270 --> 00:49:59.050
Well, I was really disappointed because I didn't get to go with Michael.
嗯，我真的很失望，因为我没能和迈克尔一起去。

1023
00:49:59.210 --> 00:50:06.770
As an actor, I wanted to see Pam take Michael to this moment in his life.
作为一名演员，我想看帕姆带迈克尔经历他生命中的这一刻。

1024
00:50:07.350 --> 00:50:09.350
But Pam refuses to go.
但帕姆拒绝去了。

1025
00:50:10.430 --> 00:50:11.950
Aaron's going to have to do it.
亚伦不得不去做了。

1026
00:50:12.090 --> 00:50:15.090
But I was very jealous as an actor.
但我作为演员真的很嫉妒。

1027
00:50:15.330 --> 00:50:19.230
That you didn't get to go spend the day with Steve and watch him do these amazing scenes.
嫉妒你没能和史蒂夫一起度过那一天，看着他表演这些精彩的戏份。

1028
00:50:19.230 --> 00:50:19.650
Yes.
是的。

1029
00:50:20.190 --> 00:50:22.510
Well, Michael now has this famous talking head.
嗯，迈克尔现在有了这个著名的访谈片段。

1030
00:50:22.590 --> 00:50:27.250
We talked about it a little bit with BJ, where he says, I just, you know, I fell in love with those kids.
我们和BJ稍微聊过这个，他说，我只是，你知道，我爱上了那些孩子。

1031
00:50:27.710 --> 00:50:29.290
And so he made him a promise.
所以他向他们许下了一个承诺。

1032
00:50:29.450 --> 00:50:30.490
He wanted to help them.
他想帮助他们。

1033
00:50:30.670 --> 00:50:34.550
He wanted to see them graduate from high school, and he would pay for their college.
他想看着他们高中毕业，并愿意资助他们的大学学费。

1034
00:50:34.550 --> 00:50:41.710
Yes, this is sort of the explanation behind this predicament, behind the premise for this episode.
是的，这算是这一集困境背后的解释，也是这一集前提的由来。

1035
00:50:41.990 --> 00:50:46.510
We got a fan question from Aaron in Oxford, Ohio, who said this.
我们收到了来自俄亥俄州牛津市亚伦的粉丝提问，他是这么说的。

1036
00:50:46.510 --> 00:50:53.590
I recently watched The Big Lebowski, and there is a specific scene that caught my eye.
我最近看了《谋杀绿脚趾》，有一个特定的场景引起了我的注意。

1037
00:50:54.010 --> 00:50:58.330
In the scene, the dude is visiting Mr. Lebowski's house.
在那个场景中，老兄去拜访勒博斯基先生的家。

1038
00:50:58.730 --> 00:51:04.450
During the visit, he's given a tour of the study and notices a picture on the wall of Mr. Lebowski
在拜访期间，他参观了书房，注意到墙上有一张勒博斯基先生的照片，

1039
00:51:04.450 --> 00:51:07.830
surrounded by a bunch of smiling high school-age children.
周围是一群微笑的高中生。

1040
00:51:07.830 --> 00:51:13.030
The dude asks, oh, are those Mr. Lebowski's children?
老兄问，哦，那些是勒博斯基先生的孩子吗？

1041
00:51:13.470 --> 00:51:17.450
To which the butler replies, they're not literally his children.
管家回答说，他们并不是他亲生的孩子。

1042
00:51:17.490 --> 00:51:22.310
They're the little Lebowski urban achievers, inner-city children of promise, but without
他们是小勒博斯基城市成就者，是来自市中心的有为青年，但缺乏

1043
00:51:22.310 --> 00:51:24.610
the necessary means for a higher education.
接受高等教育的必要经济条件。

1044
00:51:24.890 --> 00:51:28.930
So Mr. Lebowski has committed to sending all of them to college.
所以勒博斯基先生承诺资助他们所有人上大学。

1045
00:51:28.930 --> 00:51:35.710
My question is, did the writers have it in their head that Michael saw this movie, and that
我的问题是，编剧们是否认为迈克尔看过这部电影，并且

1046
00:51:35.710 --> 00:51:41.470
this might have led him to making a similar promise, or is it just a coincidence?
这是否导致他做出了类似的承诺，还是这仅仅是个巧合？

1047
00:51:42.390 --> 00:51:44.170
I had to find out.
我必须弄清楚。

1048
00:51:44.490 --> 00:51:50.530
So I reached out to Gene and Lee, who wrote this episode, and they said that the idea for
所以我联系了这一集的编剧吉恩和李，他们说这一集的构思

1049
00:51:50.530 --> 00:51:55.010
this episode actually came from Paul Lieberstein.
实际上来自保罗·利伯斯坦。

1050
00:51:55.650 --> 00:52:00.690
Paul confirmed this, and when I asked him if the idea was inspired by The Big Lebowski,
保罗证实了这一点，当我问他这个想法是否受到《谋杀绿脚趾》的启发时，

1051
00:52:00.730 --> 00:52:04.490
he said no, that he wasn't even aware of that scene in the movie.
他说没有，他甚至都不知道电影里有那一幕。

1052
00:52:05.070 --> 00:52:10.610
Paul said that there was a real story of a businessman who did this with extraordinary
保罗说，确实有个商人曾有过这样的真实故事，他在20世纪90年代

1053
00:52:10.610 --> 00:52:13.050
success back in the 1990s.
取得了非凡的成功。

1054
00:52:13.170 --> 00:52:15.270
He thinks maybe it was Chicago.
他觉得可能是在芝加哥。

1055
00:52:15.270 --> 00:52:16.690
He couldn't quite remember.
他记不太清了。

1056
00:52:17.170 --> 00:52:20.890
But it was a high school where the graduation rate was incredibly low.
但那是一所毕业率极低的高中。

1057
00:52:20.890 --> 00:52:26.370
But within the group of kids that he made this promise to, all of them went to college.
而在他许下承诺的那群孩子中，他们全都上了大学。

1058
00:52:26.850 --> 00:52:33.550
And Paul just remembered the photo in the newspaper, and he said that seems like something
保罗只记得报纸上的那张照片，他说那看起来像是

1059
00:52:33.550 --> 00:52:35.390
Michael Scott would do.
迈克尔·斯科特会做的事。

1060
00:52:35.690 --> 00:52:41.090
That Michael, because of his good heart and being so sure that he would be a millionaire
因为迈克尔心地善良，而且非常确信自己能在这些孩子毕业时

1061
00:52:41.090 --> 00:52:48.190
by the time these kids graduated, that he would want to help, and he would make this promise.
成为百万富翁，所以他会想要帮忙，并许下这个承诺。

1062
00:52:48.190 --> 00:52:53.250
He said, quote, it felt like a really honest problem coming from this character.
他说，引用原话，这感觉像是这个角色会遇到的一个非常真实的问题。

1063
00:52:53.890 --> 00:52:59.710
So that was the inspiration, was this article that he had seen of someone doing this successfully
所以灵感来源就是他看到的这篇关于某人成功做到此事的文章，

1064
00:52:59.710 --> 00:53:04.250
and thinking, Michael Scott wouldn't do it successfully, though, would he?
然后心想，迈克尔·斯科特可没法成功做到，对吧？

1065
00:53:04.250 --> 00:53:06.910
He'd want to do it, but he wouldn't be able to follow through.
他会想去做，但他没法坚持到底。

1066
00:53:07.170 --> 00:53:07.410
Yeah.
没错。

1067
00:53:07.550 --> 00:53:10.970
So he said the idea was his, but Lee and Gene made it their own.
所以他说主意是他出的，但李和吉恩把它变成了他们自己的东西。

1068
00:53:11.110 --> 00:53:13.270
They came up with the dance, the batteries.
他们想出了舞蹈和电池的桥段。

1069
00:53:13.270 --> 00:53:14.810
He said that was all them.
他说那全是他们的功劳。

1070
00:53:15.070 --> 00:53:18.950
But that was the inspiration behind Scott's Tots.
但这就是《斯科特的学童》背后的灵感来源。

1071
00:53:19.570 --> 00:53:20.170
Well, I love that.
嗯，我喜欢这个。

1072
00:53:20.250 --> 00:53:22.450
I always love finding out the inspiration for our episodes.
我总是喜欢挖掘我们剧集的灵感来源。

1073
00:53:22.850 --> 00:53:25.630
It's usually some little thing that just stuck with someone.
通常都是一些让某人印象深刻的小事。

1074
00:53:25.850 --> 00:53:26.050
Yeah.
没错。

1075
00:53:26.590 --> 00:53:31.110
Meanwhile, in the kitchen, Dwight is continuing to act strange.
与此同时，在厨房里，德怀特继续表现得很奇怪。

1076
00:53:32.170 --> 00:53:32.650
Yeah.
没错。

1077
00:53:32.650 --> 00:53:40.490
He's showering Jim with compliments, and then he provides him with a spreadsheet so that Jim
他不断地恭维吉姆，然后给了他一张电子表格，这样吉姆

1078
00:53:40.490 --> 00:53:44.830
can rank everyone based on performance for his Employee of the Month project.
就可以根据绩效为他的“月度最佳员工”项目给每个人排名。

1079
00:53:45.290 --> 00:53:51.010
He says he'll run it over to Toby and the accounting department, so it'll just be, like, totally...
他说他会把表格送到托比和会计部门，这样一切就完全……

1080
00:53:51.010 --> 00:53:51.630
Impartial.
公正了。

1081
00:53:51.770 --> 00:53:52.530
They'll run the data.
他们会处理数据。

1082
00:53:52.730 --> 00:53:53.290
Exactly.
没错。

1083
00:53:53.630 --> 00:53:54.450
Just database.
纯粹的数据处理。

1084
00:53:54.950 --> 00:53:55.170
Yeah.
没错。

1085
00:54:02.730 --> 00:54:06.010
Nothing into the kitchen is to get something out of the fridge, to run into Jim.
去厨房不是为了从冰箱里拿东西，而是为了偶遇吉姆。

1086
00:54:06.350 --> 00:54:06.870
No.
不是。

1087
00:54:07.090 --> 00:54:07.790
What was it?
那是什么？

1088
00:54:08.210 --> 00:54:08.730
Mustard.
芥末酱。

1089
00:54:09.130 --> 00:54:10.490
What's he doing with mustard?
他拿芥末酱干什么？

1090
00:54:10.750 --> 00:54:11.570
I don't know.
我不知道。

1091
00:54:11.810 --> 00:54:12.930
Did he do anything with it?
他用它做了什么吗？

1092
00:54:12.970 --> 00:54:16.810
He does nothing with the mustard, but when they pull back wide, there are more things
他什么也没用芥末酱做，但当镜头拉远时，柜台上还有更多

1093
00:54:16.810 --> 00:54:19.330
on the counter that he has gotten out of the fridge.
他从冰箱里拿出来的东西。

1094
00:54:19.750 --> 00:54:24.010
He also got out jelly and, I think, barbecue sauce.
他还拿出了果酱，我想还有烧烤酱。

1095
00:54:24.390 --> 00:54:24.910
Gross.
恶心。

1096
00:54:25.290 --> 00:54:30.030
So he's definitely, I guess, heavy in the condiments.
所以我猜他绝对是在大量使用调味品。

1097
00:54:30.030 --> 00:54:32.630
Is jelly a condiment?
果酱算是调味品吗？

1098
00:54:33.090 --> 00:54:34.610
Is jelly a condiment?
果酱是调味品吗？

1099
00:54:34.830 --> 00:54:36.450
I mean, you put it on...
我是说，你把它涂在……

1100
00:54:36.530 --> 00:54:37.550
Is butter a condiment?
黄油是调味品吗？

1101
00:54:37.870 --> 00:54:38.790
I'm going to say no.
我打算说不。

1102
00:54:38.790 --> 00:54:39.810
What is a condiment?
什么是调味品？

1103
00:54:40.410 --> 00:54:42.230
Isn't a condiment like...
调味品不就是……

1104
00:54:42.230 --> 00:54:44.210
Well, I guess, isn't it like the extras?
嗯，我想，不就是那些额外的东西吗？

1105
00:54:44.210 --> 00:54:45.290
So maybe you're right.
所以也许你是对的。

1106
00:54:45.570 --> 00:54:48.770
I mean, what is a condiment?
我是说，到底什么是调味品？

1107
00:54:49.090 --> 00:54:50.250
Like salt and pepper?
比如盐和胡椒？

1108
00:54:50.590 --> 00:54:51.730
No, that's a spice.
不，那是香料。

1109
00:54:54.150 --> 00:54:55.090
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1110
00:54:55.790 --> 00:55:01.530
The definition of condiment is a substance such as salt or ketchup that is used to add
调味品的定义是像盐或番茄酱那样，用于增加

1111
00:55:01.530 --> 00:55:02.710
flavor to food.
食物风味的物质。

1112
00:55:02.850 --> 00:55:03.530
Thank you.
谢谢你。

1113
00:55:03.730 --> 00:55:05.390
Spices are condiments?
香料也是调味品吗？

1114
00:55:05.750 --> 00:55:07.850
Look who was right about something.
看看是谁说对了。

1115
00:55:08.310 --> 00:55:12.710
I found a chart that lists the calories in different condiments.
我找到了一张列出不同调味品热量的图表。

1116
00:55:12.890 --> 00:55:15.510
Did you know honey is considered a condiment?
你知道蜂蜜也被视为调味品吗？

1117
00:55:15.730 --> 00:55:16.830
Well, that makes sense now.
嗯，现在说得通了。

1118
00:55:17.470 --> 00:55:20.290
They're listing marinara as a condiment.
他们把意面酱也列为调味品。

1119
00:55:20.510 --> 00:55:21.890
It enhances flavor.
它能提升风味。

1120
00:55:22.590 --> 00:55:24.530
Everything enhances flavor.
什么东西都能提升风味。

1121
00:55:24.530 --> 00:55:26.910
An onion enhances flavor.
洋葱也能提升风味。

1122
00:55:27.130 --> 00:55:27.470
Garlic.
大蒜也是。

1123
00:55:28.230 --> 00:55:30.130
Does it have to be...
它必须是……

1124
00:55:30.130 --> 00:55:32.070
Do you have to squeeze it out of a bottle?
它必须是从瓶子里挤出来的吗？

1125
00:55:32.270 --> 00:55:32.990
Does it have to be...
它必须是……

1126
00:55:32.990 --> 00:55:33.130
Yeah.
没错。

1127
00:55:33.510 --> 00:55:34.610
Does it have to be in something?
它必须装在什么东西里吗？

1128
00:55:35.570 --> 00:55:37.070
What is a condiment?
什么是调味品？

1129
00:55:37.450 --> 00:55:39.390
I need more information.
我需要更多信息。

1130
00:55:39.710 --> 00:55:41.330
We need more information on condiments.
我们需要更多关于调味品的信息。

1131
00:55:42.030 --> 00:55:42.910
Hold on.
等等。

1132
00:55:43.230 --> 00:55:46.330
Is jelly a condiment?
果冻是调味品吗？

1133
00:55:47.870 --> 00:55:53.510
Jelly and jam are usually viewed as condiments, but peanut butter is not.
果冻和果酱通常被视为调味品，但花生酱不是。

1134
00:55:54.770 --> 00:55:59.390
Salsa is considered a condiment, but guacamole is not.
莎莎酱被视为调味品，但牛油果酱不是。

1135
00:55:59.590 --> 00:56:00.310
Here's what I'm thinking.
我是这么想的。

1136
00:56:00.470 --> 00:56:04.810
Condiments either have to be something you sprinkle or like kind of more of a liquidy form.
调味品要么是你撒上去的东西，要么是某种液态形式的东西。

1137
00:56:05.230 --> 00:56:11.850
Not according to Wikipedia, which says a condiment is a supplemental food such as a sauce or powder.
维基百科可不是这么说的，它说调味品是像酱汁或粉末之类的补充性食物。

1138
00:56:13.230 --> 00:56:14.430
Sprinkle and liquid.
撒上去的和液体的。

1139
00:56:15.230 --> 00:56:16.610
That supports my theory.
这支持了我的理论。

1140
00:56:17.710 --> 00:56:20.230
If it's more of a solid substance, it's not a condiment.
如果它是固体物质，那它就不是调味品。

1141
00:56:20.510 --> 00:56:22.690
If you can sprinkle it or pour it, it's a condiment.
如果你能撒它或倒它，它就是调味品。

1142
00:56:22.690 --> 00:56:24.650
If you can chop it, it's not a condiment.
如果你能切它，它就不是调味品。

1143
00:56:25.330 --> 00:56:26.350
Sprinkle and pour.
撒和倒。

1144
00:56:26.910 --> 00:56:27.530
All right.
好吧。

1145
00:56:27.710 --> 00:56:29.830
Are we ready to move on from the condiments?
我们准备好结束调味品这个话题了吗？

1146
00:56:30.790 --> 00:56:31.230
Maybe.
也许吧。

1147
00:56:31.670 --> 00:56:32.090
Oh, no.
噢，不。

1148
00:56:33.830 --> 00:56:35.370
My God, you're making a lot of...
天哪，你弄出了好多……

1149
00:56:35.370 --> 00:56:36.290
It sounds like...
听起来像是……

1150
00:56:36.290 --> 00:56:36.610
You know what?
你知道吗？

1151
00:56:36.730 --> 00:56:37.270
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1152
00:56:37.270 --> 00:56:37.870
I'm sorry.
抱歉。

1153
00:56:37.990 --> 00:56:39.950
When you do that, hmm, it means you disagree.
当你发出那种声音时，嗯，意味着你不同意。

1154
00:56:40.350 --> 00:56:40.770
Like, hmm.
比如，嗯。

1155
00:56:41.550 --> 00:56:42.030
Icing.
糖霜。

1156
00:56:43.110 --> 00:56:44.630
Icing is a condiment?
糖霜是调味品吗？

1157
00:56:44.950 --> 00:56:49.150
So when I'm eating a cupcake, I'm eating cake with a condiment on top?
所以当我吃纸杯蛋糕时，我是在吃上面加了调味品的蛋糕？

1158
00:56:49.290 --> 00:56:50.250
Makes sense to me.
我觉得说得通。

1159
00:56:50.810 --> 00:56:51.290
Really?
真的吗？

1160
00:56:51.830 --> 00:56:52.810
Jenna's doing it.
珍娜就在这么做。

1161
00:56:52.930 --> 00:56:53.190
Hmm.
嗯。

1162
00:56:53.470 --> 00:56:54.390
I knew it.
我就知道。

1163
00:56:56.560 --> 00:57:03.100
If you're ever in a conversation with Jenna and she goes, hmm, it means she is slightly judging you and disagrees.
如果你和珍娜聊天时她发出“嗯”的声音，那就意味着她在暗自评判你，并且不同意你的观点。

1164
00:57:03.460 --> 00:57:05.740
Well, Wikipedia says peanut butter is a condiment.
好吧，维基百科说花生酱是调味品。

1165
00:57:05.740 --> 00:57:08.020
So clearly, I don't know.
所以显然，我也不清楚。

1166
00:57:08.280 --> 00:57:09.340
Clearly, there's a debate.
显然，这还有争议。

1167
00:57:09.860 --> 00:57:13.980
So Dwight has put a bunch of random condiments on the counter.
所以德怀特在柜台上放了一堆乱七八糟的调味品。

1168
00:57:14.240 --> 00:57:14.760
He has.
确实放了。

1169
00:57:15.260 --> 00:57:16.880
And I have nowhere to go from there.
然后我就没法接话了。

1170
00:57:16.980 --> 00:57:17.640
That's the end.
话题到此为止。

1171
00:57:18.400 --> 00:57:19.480
We can move on.
我们可以继续了。

1172
00:57:19.660 --> 00:57:22.100
He clearly isn't intending on doing anything with them.
他显然没打算用它们做什么。

1173
00:57:22.180 --> 00:57:25.620
He's just doing busy work so he can set up gym to fail.
他只是在装忙，好让吉姆出丑。

1174
00:57:26.040 --> 00:57:30.160
Next up, Michael and Erin are going to arrive at the high school.
接下来，迈克尔和艾琳要到达高中了。

1175
00:57:30.300 --> 00:57:33.040
And I have a little location breakdown for you.
我为你们准备了一点拍摄地点的介绍。

1176
00:57:33.040 --> 00:57:40.040
So fan question from Cyrus in Bloomfield, Michigan, were the school scenes filmed at a local L.A.
来自密歇根州布卢姆菲尔德的赛勒斯的粉丝提问：学校的场景是在洛杉矶当地的学校拍摄的吗？

1177
00:57:40.180 --> 00:57:40.460
school?
学校？

1178
00:57:41.140 --> 00:57:42.240
Yes, they were.
是的，确实是。

1179
00:57:42.540 --> 00:57:50.580
We shot the interiors and exteriors at Van Nuys Middle School, which is a steam magnet school on Vesper Avenue in Van Nuys, California.
我们在范奈斯中学拍摄了室内和室外场景，那是一所位于加州范奈斯维斯珀大道的STEAM磁力学校。

1180
00:57:51.120 --> 00:57:55.920
We were there for two days, Monday and Tuesday, October 3rd and 4th.
我们在那里待了两天，10月3日和4日，周一和周二。

1181
00:57:55.920 --> 00:58:01.400
By the way, this is also where they shot the school location for the TV show Fresh Off the Boat.
顺便说一下，这也是电视剧《初来乍到》拍摄学校场景的地方。

1182
00:58:01.700 --> 00:58:04.200
Well, I had a recurring guest star on Fresh Off the Boat.
嗯，我在《初来乍到》里演过常驻客串角色。

1183
00:58:04.620 --> 00:58:06.240
Do you know if you ever went to the school?
你知道你有没有去过那所学校吗？

1184
00:58:06.440 --> 00:58:09.200
I think we did one day because I was at a PTA meeting.
我想我们去过一天，因为我当时在参加家长会。

1185
00:58:09.480 --> 00:58:13.300
I was like the mean lady shocker.
我演的是那个刻薄的女人，真让人吃惊。

1186
00:58:15.460 --> 00:58:18.540
Well, there's a lot of great little details at this school.
这所学校里有很多很棒的小细节。

1187
00:58:18.720 --> 00:58:20.020
Phil Shea outdid himself.
菲尔·谢伊真是超常发挥了。

1188
00:58:20.200 --> 00:58:23.440
I loved the plaque that said Michael Gary Scott Reading Room.
我很喜欢那块写着“迈克尔·加里·斯科特阅览室”的牌匾。

1189
00:58:23.980 --> 00:58:25.900
And Erin's like, you're famous.
艾琳当时说，你出名了。

1190
00:58:26.320 --> 00:58:26.760
Yes.
是的。

1191
00:58:27.200 --> 00:58:33.160
Michael has cold feet about seeing everyone, but Mikayla greets them and insists they just want to give them a big thank you.
迈克尔对见到大家感到退缩，但米凯拉迎接了他们，并坚持说他们只是想好好感谢他。

1192
00:58:33.400 --> 00:58:34.080
I know.
我知道。

1193
00:58:34.700 --> 00:58:36.980
Mikayla was played by Eshiba Renee.
米凯拉由埃希巴·雷内饰演。

1194
00:58:37.520 --> 00:58:41.920
She posted on Instagram that she still has her shirt from this episode.
她在Instagram上发帖说，她还留着这一集里的那件衬衫。

1195
00:58:41.920 --> 00:58:44.020
Oh, she got to keep her Scott's Tots shirt.
哦，她能留下那件“斯科特的小伙伴”衬衫。

1196
00:58:44.080 --> 00:58:44.840
That's so cool.
太酷了。

1197
00:58:45.000 --> 00:58:46.000
She was so good.
她演得真好。

1198
00:58:46.300 --> 00:58:53.880
And she is going to lead Michael into this classroom full of kids all wearing Scott's Tots shirts.
她要把迈克尔带进那间满是穿着“斯科特的小伙伴”衬衫的孩子们的教室。

1199
00:58:54.260 --> 00:58:55.920
I mean, huge applause.
我是说，掌声雷动。

1200
00:58:56.140 --> 00:58:57.540
They're so excited he's there.
他们太兴奋他能来了。

1201
00:58:57.860 --> 00:59:05.980
We find out that they have prepared something for him, which is a song and dance routine.
我们发现他们为他准备了一些节目，是一段歌舞表演。

1202
00:59:06.700 --> 00:59:10.580
We had a fan question from Harmjen V in the Netherlands.
我们收到了一位来自荷兰的粉丝 Harmjen V 的提问。

1203
00:59:11.220 --> 00:59:14.640
The dance routine of the Tots is awesome.
“小不点”们的舞蹈动作太棒了。

1204
00:59:15.340 --> 00:59:17.620
Where did you find these actors' dancers?
你们是从哪里找到这些演员兼舞者的？

1205
00:59:18.040 --> 00:59:21.980
And Lisa from New Jersey asked who choreographed the dance routine.
来自新泽西州的丽莎问是谁编排的这段舞蹈。

1206
00:59:22.460 --> 00:59:26.600
Well, Randy Cordray shared with us that the choreographer was Tony Gonzalez.
兰迪·科德雷告诉我们，编舞是托尼·冈萨雷斯。

1207
00:59:27.200 --> 00:59:31.820
And he had done choreography for Bring It On Again and Bring It On All or Nothing.
他曾为《魅力四射2：再次出击》和《魅力四射4：无论如何》担任编舞。

1208
00:59:31.820 --> 00:59:35.540
You know, he's currently doing the choreography for The Masked Singer.
你知道吗，他目前正在为《蒙面歌王》担任编舞。

1209
00:59:36.180 --> 00:59:39.320
And he cast the eight specialty dancers.
他挑选了八位专业舞者。

1210
00:59:39.980 --> 00:59:42.820
The dancers were Danielle E.
这些舞者分别是丹妮尔·E。

1211
00:59:42.920 --> 00:59:51.780
Hawkins, Glenda Morales, David Easel, Katrina Norman, Chris Moss, Oscar Orozco, Jonathan Rice, and Quentin Burdett.
霍金斯、格伦达·莫拉莱斯、大卫·伊塞尔、卡特里娜·诺曼、克里斯·莫斯、奥斯卡·奥罗斯科、乔纳森·赖斯和昆汀·伯德特。

1212
00:59:51.780 --> 00:59:55.320
But we only had two days of rehearsals with the dancers.
但我们和舞者们只有两天的排练时间。

1213
00:59:55.860 --> 00:59:59.320
They set up a rehearsal space over on our warehouse stage.
他们在我们的仓库舞台那边搭建了一个排练场地。

1214
00:59:59.740 --> 01:00:01.100
They were so good.
他们太棒了。

1215
01:00:01.260 --> 01:00:02.340
They were so good.
他们真的太棒了。

1216
01:00:02.560 --> 01:00:07.200
There's no way in a million years that I could learn anything like that in two days.
我这辈子都不可能在两天内学会那样的舞蹈。

1217
01:00:07.620 --> 01:00:08.080
No.
不可能。

1218
01:00:08.320 --> 01:00:09.220
It's just a gift.
这真的是一种天赋。

1219
01:00:09.400 --> 01:00:10.120
You just have it.
你就是有这种天赋。

1220
01:00:10.440 --> 01:00:13.300
You know, I danced growing up.
你知道，我从小就跳舞。

1221
01:00:13.620 --> 01:00:16.100
There was a time when I could do that.
曾经有一段时间我也能做到那样。

1222
01:00:16.260 --> 01:00:17.620
That time is not now anymore.
但现在已经不行了。

1223
01:00:18.340 --> 01:00:21.840
I tried during the pandemic to take up my tap dancing again.
疫情期间我试着重新开始练习踢踏舞。

1224
01:00:22.120 --> 01:00:23.520
I got a little tap dance floor.
我买了一块小小的踢踏舞地板。

1225
01:00:23.720 --> 01:00:24.180
I remember this.
我记得这件事。

1226
01:00:24.620 --> 01:00:25.400
And I was tapping.
我当时在练踢踏舞。

1227
01:00:26.060 --> 01:00:30.300
And I thought, I'm going to learn a tap routine to footloose.
我想，我要学一段《浑身是劲》的踢踏舞。

1228
01:00:30.560 --> 01:00:30.980
Oh.
噢。

1229
01:00:32.180 --> 01:00:32.620
And.
然后。

1230
01:00:32.840 --> 01:00:34.260
Like, you got to cut loose.
就像歌里唱的，你要彻底释放。

1231
01:00:34.280 --> 01:00:34.540
Yeah.
是啊。

1232
01:00:34.680 --> 01:00:35.040
Foot, okay.
脚，好吧。

1233
01:00:35.180 --> 01:00:38.300
And I found, like, an instructional video on YouTube.
我在 YouTube 上找了一个教学视频。

1234
01:00:39.060 --> 01:00:41.460
And I was like, this is going to be great.
当时我想，这肯定很棒。

1235
01:00:41.620 --> 01:00:42.860
It's going to be so fun.
一定会很有趣。

1236
01:00:43.040 --> 01:00:45.320
I mean, it was, like, 45 seconds long.
我是说，那段舞只有 45 秒长。

1237
01:00:46.340 --> 01:00:46.780
Weeks.
几周。

1238
01:00:47.300 --> 01:00:49.900
Weeks I spent on this very beginner tap routine.
我花了几周时间才学会这个非常基础的踢踏舞动作。

1239
01:00:50.160 --> 01:00:51.500
I never posted it.
我从来没发出来过。

1240
01:00:51.620 --> 01:00:55.840
I have, like, a gazillion videos of myself in my garage on my tap floor.
我的车库里有无数段自己在踢踏舞地板上跳舞的视频。

1241
01:00:56.100 --> 01:00:56.960
Can I please see one?
我能看一段吗？

1242
01:00:57.000 --> 01:00:58.380
Can I please put it in pod stories?
我可以把它放进播客的故事里吗？

1243
01:00:59.500 --> 01:01:01.120
Not to laugh at you.
不是为了嘲笑你。

1244
01:01:01.420 --> 01:01:02.600
Not to laugh at you.
真的不是为了嘲笑你。

1245
01:01:02.720 --> 01:01:05.840
To laugh with me because I was not even laughing yet.
是为了和我一起笑，因为我当时还没笑出来呢。

1246
01:01:06.120 --> 01:01:06.600
So.
所以。

1247
01:01:07.520 --> 01:01:08.400
Someone's laughing.
有人在笑。

1248
01:01:09.420 --> 01:01:09.900
Maybe.
也许吧。

1249
01:01:10.280 --> 01:01:10.660
Maybe.
也许。

1250
01:01:10.920 --> 01:01:11.340
Okay.
好吧。

1251
01:01:11.640 --> 01:01:14.100
Well, I thought the dancers did a fantastic job.
嗯，我觉得舞者们表现得太棒了。

1252
01:01:14.240 --> 01:01:14.780
They did.
确实如此。

1253
01:01:16.780 --> 01:01:20.440
We had a grand question from Laura in Warren, Ohio, who said, who wrote the song?
我们收到了一位来自俄亥俄州沃伦市的劳拉提出的一个很棒的问题，她问，这首歌是谁写的？

1254
01:01:20.560 --> 01:01:21.640
Hey, Mr. Scott.
《嘿，斯科特先生》。

1255
01:01:22.440 --> 01:01:27.040
Well, Lee and Jean wrote the lyrics for the song, and Eve Nelson wrote the music.
嗯，李和简负责填词，伊芙·尼尔森负责谱曲。

1256
01:01:27.640 --> 01:01:33.920
Eve is an Emmy-winning composer who did a lot of specialty work for us, such as composing
伊芙是一位获得过艾美奖的作曲家，她为我们做了很多特别的工作，比如创作了

1257
01:01:33.920 --> 01:01:37.580
the music for Subtle Sexuality, the webisode.
网络剧《微妙的性取向》的配乐。

1258
01:01:37.580 --> 01:01:39.080
The one we listened to last week.
就是我们上周听的那部。

1259
01:01:39.160 --> 01:01:40.780
Yes, that Mindy sings.
对，明迪唱的那部。

1260
01:01:41.540 --> 01:01:44.260
She also did all the music for Threat Level Midnight.
她还为《威胁等级午夜》创作了所有的音乐。

1261
01:01:44.680 --> 01:01:48.040
I thought we should hear an audio clip of Hey, Mr. Scott.
我想我们应该听听《嘿，斯科特先生》的音频片段。

1262
01:01:48.460 --> 01:01:48.680
Ooh.
噢。

1263
01:02:27.120 --> 01:02:28.800
So good, Eve Nelson.
太棒了，伊芙·尼尔森。

1264
01:02:29.060 --> 01:02:30.340
Eve coming through again.
伊芙再次展现了实力。

1265
01:02:30.340 --> 01:02:32.580
And I can't wait now to see Threat Level Midnight.
我现在迫不及待想看《威胁等级午夜》了。

1266
01:02:32.720 --> 01:02:33.140
I know.
我知道。

1267
01:02:33.260 --> 01:02:34.080
And see all that music.
还能听到所有那些音乐。

1268
01:02:34.540 --> 01:02:38.320
It's funny that you bring up the webisodes because just last week we were talking about
你提到网络剧真有意思，因为就在上周我们还在聊这个，但我上周也提到了摇头娃娃的事，就是当时在NBC.com工作的乔亚·巴尔福说要带这些摇头娃娃到片场，对吧？

1269
01:02:38.320 --> 01:02:43.120
it, but I also mentioned the bobbleheads last week that Joya Balfour, who worked for
对。

1270
01:02:43.120 --> 01:02:47.100
NBC.com, was going to bring all these bobbleheads to the set, right?
为了让我能在《安吉拉历险记》里展示它们。

1271
01:02:47.220 --> 01:02:47.440
Yeah.
那天在片场，有位女士对我说，安吉拉，你想要这些摇头娃娃吗？

1272
01:02:47.580 --> 01:02:49.420
For me to feature in Adventures with Angela.
她说，既然你在为我们做这个，你可以拥有所有演员的摇头娃娃。

1273
01:02:50.020 --> 01:02:54.060
Lady on set that day, she said, Angela, would you like all of these bobbleheads?
我说，天哪，我当然想要。

1274
01:02:54.760 --> 01:02:57.720
Like, you can have one of all the cast members since you're doing this for us.
她说，好的，让我看看。

1275
01:02:57.800 --> 01:02:58.880
And I said, oh my God, I would.
我想我能给你弄到一套完整的演员摇头娃娃。

1276
01:02:58.940 --> 01:03:00.540
And she goes, okay, let me see.
我说，噢，那太有趣了。

1277
01:03:00.620 --> 01:03:04.360
But I think I can get you a whole set of full cast member bobbleheads.
也许我可以把它们排成一排放在我家的架子上。

1278
01:03:04.620 --> 01:03:06.120
And I was like, oh, that'll be so fun.
那太酷了。

1279
01:03:06.180 --> 01:03:08.960
Maybe I'll like line them like on a shelf in my house.
你有它们吗？

1280
01:03:09.080 --> 01:03:09.860
That is so cool.
好的。

1281
01:03:09.980 --> 01:03:10.580
Do you have them?
事情是这样的。

1282
01:03:10.800 --> 01:03:11.080
Okay.
几年前，她说，安吉拉，我给你弄到摇头娃娃了。

1283
01:03:11.080 --> 01:03:11.940
So here's the thing.
你什么时候想要？

1284
01:03:12.120 --> 01:03:14.740
Years ago, she was like, Angela, I got the bobbleheads for you.
当时我正好在搬家。

1285
01:03:14.820 --> 01:03:15.340
When do you want them?
我说，噢，我正好在搬家。

1286
01:03:15.420 --> 01:03:16.300
And I was moving.
我们能再商量吗？

1287
01:03:16.700 --> 01:03:18.460
And I was like, oh, I'm moving right now.
然后，珍娜，我也不知道。

1288
01:03:18.640 --> 01:03:19.420
Can we figure out?
生活琐事缠身。

1289
01:03:19.700 --> 01:03:20.580
And Jenna, I don't know.
几年过去了。

1290
01:03:20.700 --> 01:03:21.340
Life happened.
乔亚联系我说，安吉拉，这些摇头娃娃我在手里放了15年了。

1291
01:03:21.860 --> 01:03:22.600
Years went by.
什么？

1292
01:03:23.000 --> 01:03:27.540
Joya reached out to me and said, Angela, I've had these bobbleheads for 15 years.
就是最近她才联系我。

1293
01:03:27.740 --> 01:03:27.940
What?
她说，它们一直装在盒子里。

1294
01:03:28.240 --> 01:03:30.100
Like just recently she reached out.
我可以给你送过去吗？

1295
01:03:30.100 --> 01:03:31.500
She was like, they're in boxes.
我说，天哪，乔亚，当然可以。

1296
01:03:32.140 --> 01:03:33.220
Can I bring them to you?
于是我们约了喝咖啡，聊了聊这15年来的生活、婚姻和孩子。

1297
01:03:33.280 --> 01:03:35.700
I said, oh my gosh, Joya, yes.
然后，珍娜，她打开后备箱，里面全是摇头娃娃。

1298
01:03:35.700 --> 01:03:41.000
So we met for coffee and we caught up 15 years of life and marriage and kids.
我拍了一张她站在后备箱旁边的照片。

1299
01:03:41.220 --> 01:03:44.620
And Jenna, she opened up her trunk and it was full of bobbleheads.
那太酷了。

1300
01:03:44.900 --> 01:03:47.220
I took a picture of her standing by her trunk.
那太酷了。

1301
01:03:47.400 --> 01:03:50.480
I now have all of these bobbleheads.
我现在拥有所有这些摇头娃娃了。

1302
01:03:50.940 --> 01:03:54.580
That is so crazy because, you know, when we were going through all of our bins of stuff
这太疯狂了，因为你知道，当我们整理那些装东西的箱子时，

1303
01:03:54.580 --> 01:04:02.700
for the book, I found an Oscar bobblehead and a Jim bobblehead and a Pam bobblehead and
为了写书，我找到了奥斯卡、吉姆、帕姆的摇头娃娃，还有

1304
01:04:02.700 --> 01:04:04.360
a Dwight bobblehead.
德怀特的摇头娃娃。

1305
01:04:04.480 --> 01:04:05.260
That's all I have.
我就只有这些。

1306
01:04:05.700 --> 01:04:09.360
I will tell you the bobblehead I didn't know I need, but I definitely needed, was Phyllis.
我得告诉你，我之前不知道自己需要，但绝对需要的一个摇头娃娃，是菲利斯的。

1307
01:04:09.760 --> 01:04:10.960
Oh, is Phyllis' good?
哦，菲利斯的那个很好吗？

1308
01:04:11.120 --> 01:04:12.200
Phyllis' is so great.
菲利斯的那个棒极了。

1309
01:04:12.840 --> 01:04:17.100
Joya went on to tell me while we were having coffee, she said, you know, it's kind of crazy.
乔亚接着告诉我，当时我们正在喝咖啡，她说，你知道，这有点疯狂。

1310
01:04:17.140 --> 01:04:21.240
I've had all these bobbleheads, but I also have something that I think a lot of people
我拥有所有这些摇头娃娃，但我还有一样东西，我想很多人

1311
01:04:21.240 --> 01:04:22.840
wanted, but I ended up getting.
都想要，但我最终得到了它。

1312
01:04:23.060 --> 01:04:24.340
And I was like, do tell.
我就说，快讲讲。

1313
01:04:25.160 --> 01:04:27.760
Guess who has the original unicorn Barbie?
猜猜谁有最初版的独角兽芭比娃娃？

1314
01:04:28.880 --> 01:04:29.240
What?
什么？

1315
01:04:29.580 --> 01:04:29.940
Yes.
没错。

1316
01:04:30.120 --> 01:04:31.760
And here's Joya sharing about it.
这就是乔亚分享的故事。

1317
01:04:31.760 --> 01:04:36.700
The story of how I acquired the Princess Unicorn Barbie doll is really fun.
我获得独角兽公主芭比娃娃的过程真的很有趣。

1318
01:04:36.700 --> 01:04:42.080
I, of course, was the digital producer for the show working at NBC.
我当时当然是NBC剧集的数字制作人。

1319
01:04:42.700 --> 01:04:48.880
And I had read the script for Moroccan Christmas, the episode that it appeared in, and I wanted
我读过《摩洛哥圣诞节》那一集的剧本，也就是它出现的那一集，我想

1320
01:04:48.880 --> 01:04:51.760
to use it for our Dunder Mifflin Infinity virtual game.
把它用到我们的“邓德·米福林无限”虚拟游戏中。

1321
01:04:51.780 --> 01:04:58.440
And I also wanted to build a website for Princess Unicorn because it seemed like this crazy, funny
我还想为独角兽公主建一个网站，因为它看起来是个疯狂又有趣的东西，

1322
