1474
01:12:16.060 --> 01:12:17.420
Who's second on the list?
名单上第二名是谁？

1475
01:12:17.440 --> 01:12:19.320
We need the second person on the liSt.
我们需要名单上的第二个人。

1476
01:12:19.960 --> 01:12:20.680
Uh-oh.
呃哦。

1477
01:12:20.680 --> 01:12:22.700
So, it's Jim's wife, Pam.
所以，是吉姆的妻子帕姆。

1478
01:12:23.080 --> 01:12:23.920
Oh, boy.
噢，天哪。

1479
01:12:24.280 --> 01:12:25.980
How is that even possible?
这怎么可能呢？

1480
01:12:26.760 --> 01:12:30.200
But Pam is going to defend herself as the winner.
但帕姆要为自己作为获胜者辩护。

1481
01:12:30.600 --> 01:12:31.760
Yeah, she's like, no, wait.
是的，她就像是，不，等等。

1482
01:12:31.900 --> 01:12:32.260
Come on.
拜托。

1483
01:12:32.340 --> 01:12:33.140
I didn't miss a date.
我没有缺勤过。

1484
01:12:33.300 --> 01:12:34.000
I came in early.
我早早来上班。

1485
01:12:34.140 --> 01:12:34.740
I stayed late.
我加班到很晚。

1486
01:12:34.900 --> 01:12:36.620
And I doubled my sales last month.
而且我上个月的销售额翻了一番。

1487
01:12:36.800 --> 01:12:37.080
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1488
01:12:37.440 --> 01:12:38.500
Andy goes, oh, really?
安迪说，噢，真的吗？

1489
01:12:38.640 --> 01:12:38.960
From what?
从多少翻到多少？

1490
01:12:39.060 --> 01:12:39.560
Two to four?
从两单变成四单？

1491
01:12:40.060 --> 01:12:40.380
Yup.
没错。

1492
01:12:40.920 --> 01:12:42.640
That is one of your most famous memes.
那是你最著名的表情包之一。

1493
01:12:43.100 --> 01:12:44.700
I have texted it to people.
我给别人发过这个表情包。

1494
01:12:45.020 --> 01:12:47.220
I have texted my own meme to people.
我甚至给自己发过我自己的表情包。

1495
01:12:47.400 --> 01:12:47.740
The yup.
就是那个“没错”。

1496
01:12:47.920 --> 01:12:50.120
I have texted an Angela eye roll to people.
我给别人发过安吉拉翻白眼的表情包。

1497
01:12:50.760 --> 01:12:51.600
My own meme.
我自己的表情包。

1498
01:12:51.800 --> 01:12:53.440
I see that yup everywhere, Jenna.
我到处都能看到那个“没错”，珍娜。

1499
01:12:53.700 --> 01:12:54.140
I know.
我知道。

1500
01:12:54.300 --> 01:12:55.220
And it's so perfect.
而且它太完美了。

1501
01:12:55.460 --> 01:12:56.580
It made me laugh.
这让我笑了。

1502
01:12:56.700 --> 01:12:59.300
Even though I know it, it still made me laugh.
即使我知道内容，它还是让我笑了。

1503
01:12:59.480 --> 01:13:01.560
It made me laugh while I was doing it.
我在做这件事的时候就笑了。

1504
01:13:01.720 --> 01:13:07.100
You'd be surprised how difficult it was to get just one word without me breaking.
你可能想不到，要说出一个词而不笑场有多难。

1505
01:13:07.520 --> 01:13:07.920
Yup.
没错。

1506
01:13:08.340 --> 01:13:08.780
Mm-hmm.
嗯。

1507
01:13:09.320 --> 01:13:10.900
Well, it's going to get even worse.
好吧，情况还会变得更糟。

1508
01:13:11.060 --> 01:13:14.720
You think it can't get worse for Jim, but now there's going to be a cake delivered with
你以为吉姆的情况不会再糟了，但现在要送来一个蛋糕，

1509
01:13:14.720 --> 01:13:15.800
his face on it.
上面印着他的脸。

1510
01:13:15.800 --> 01:13:17.820
This was a real cake, you guys.
伙计们，这可是个真蛋糕。

1511
01:13:18.040 --> 01:13:19.660
We actually ate this cake.
我们真的吃了这个蛋糕。

1512
01:13:19.800 --> 01:13:20.120
We did.
确实吃了。

1513
01:13:20.360 --> 01:13:21.560
I had a slice of it.
我吃了一块。

1514
01:13:21.820 --> 01:13:23.080
It was delicious.
味道很棒。

1515
01:13:23.600 --> 01:13:27.540
It was a real distorted angle of John's face.
那是约翰脸部一个非常扭曲的角度。

1516
01:13:27.700 --> 01:13:28.540
It was a little bit.
确实有点。

1517
01:13:28.580 --> 01:13:32.640
It was like when someone takes a photo of you and they go like chin up.
就像有人给你拍照时让你把下巴抬起来一样。

1518
01:13:33.880 --> 01:13:38.120
I actually had my camera on set that day and I took a picture of the cake.
那天我正好带了相机在片场，我就拍了那张蛋糕的照片。

1519
01:13:38.200 --> 01:13:39.440
I'll put it in stories.
我会把它发到快拍里。

1520
01:13:40.480 --> 01:13:47.280
The cake delivery man was played by Charlie Sanders, who is a writer, actor, and co-producer
送蛋糕的人是由查理·桑德斯饰演的，他是一位编剧、演员，也是

1521
01:13:47.280 --> 01:13:53.020
of Key and Peele, for which he was nominated for an Emmy for Outstanding Writing three years
《基和皮尔》的联合制片人，他曾凭借该剧连续三年获得艾美奖最佳编剧提名。

1522
01:13:53.020 --> 01:13:53.460
in a row.
连续三年。

1523
01:13:53.740 --> 01:13:55.040
I love Key and Peele.
我喜欢《基和皮尔》。

1524
01:13:55.200 --> 01:13:55.700
Me too.
我也是。

1525
01:13:56.080 --> 01:13:57.440
Oh my God, it cracks me up.
天哪，他们太搞笑了。

1526
01:13:57.520 --> 01:13:58.720
We hung out with Key and Peele.
我们和基和皮尔一起玩过。

1527
01:13:58.780 --> 01:13:59.240
We did.
确实。

1528
01:13:59.340 --> 01:14:01.220
We were on a private plane with them.
我们和他们一起坐过私人飞机。

1529
01:14:01.300 --> 01:14:03.080
The only time I've ever been on a private plane.
那是我唯一一次坐私人飞机。

1530
01:14:03.240 --> 01:14:03.940
Well, same.
我也是。

1531
01:14:04.820 --> 01:14:10.660
Yes, Caesar Palace flew Jenna and Keegan and Jordan to play in this poker tournament.
是的，凯撒皇宫酒店邀请了珍娜、基根和乔丹去参加扑克锦标赛。

1532
01:14:10.900 --> 01:14:12.080
You took me as a plus one.
你带我作为你的随行人员去了。

1533
01:14:12.200 --> 01:14:13.720
They flew us to New Orleans.
他们把我们飞到了新奥尔良。

1534
01:14:14.060 --> 01:14:18.920
We got on this private plane with these guys and we played Euchre the whole plane ride.
我们和这些人一起上了私人飞机，整个航程都在玩尤克牌。

1535
01:14:19.140 --> 01:14:20.480
I love Euchre.
我喜欢尤克牌。

1536
01:14:20.640 --> 01:14:22.620
We couldn't believe other people knew Euchre.
我们简直不敢相信还有别人会玩尤克牌。

1537
01:14:22.960 --> 01:14:24.040
It's a card game.
那是一种纸牌游戏。

1538
01:14:24.220 --> 01:14:24.860
We love them.
我们很喜欢他们。

1539
01:14:24.980 --> 01:14:25.540
They're so fun.
他们太有趣了。

1540
01:14:26.060 --> 01:14:29.880
The cake is not the last thing on Dwight's list of diabolical plans.
蛋糕并不是德怀特邪恶计划清单上的最后一项。

1541
01:14:29.880 --> 01:14:35.680
No, he riles everybody up, but it only works if people complain to David Wallace.
不，他煽动了所有人，但这只有在人们向大卫·华莱士投诉时才有效。

1542
01:14:36.160 --> 01:14:41.940
So Dwight starts calling David Wallace's office, pretending to be everyone else.
所以德怀特开始给大卫·华莱士的办公室打电话，假装成其他人。

1543
01:14:42.060 --> 01:14:43.180
It's so good.
太精彩了。

1544
01:14:43.540 --> 01:14:45.880
I actually, I thought we needed to hear it.
我其实觉得我们应该听听看。

1545
01:14:45.980 --> 01:14:51.480
He is going to leave messages as Kevin, as Stanley, and as Toby.
他会模仿凯文、斯坦利和托比留下语音留言。

1546
01:14:51.820 --> 01:14:54.960
I think my favorite part is like his body language.
我觉得我最喜欢的部分是他的肢体语言。

1547
01:14:55.100 --> 01:14:55.500
Changes.
会跟着变。

1548
01:14:55.800 --> 01:14:59.680
As he's doing all the voice, he's like spinning his hair with his fingertip
当他模仿那些声音时，他会用指尖绕着头发，

1549
01:14:59.680 --> 01:15:00.680
when he's being Toby.
就像他在模仿托比的时候那样。

1550
01:15:01.000 --> 01:15:01.160
Yeah.
没错。

1551
01:15:01.300 --> 01:15:02.740
He's like all slumped on the ground.
他整个人瘫倒在地上。

1552
01:15:02.940 --> 01:15:03.060
Yeah.
是啊。

1553
01:15:03.420 --> 01:15:04.300
But here it is.
但重点在这儿。

1554
01:15:04.400 --> 01:15:05.080
You have to hear it.
你一定要听听看。

1555
01:15:05.920 --> 01:15:07.340
This is Kevin Malone.
这是凯文·马龙。

1556
01:15:07.640 --> 01:15:08.640
Is David there?
大卫在吗？

1557
01:15:09.300 --> 01:15:10.660
No, he's on his weekly staff meeting.
不在，他正在开每周员工例会。

1558
01:15:10.760 --> 01:15:11.360
Can I take a message?
需要我转达什么吗？

1559
01:15:11.940 --> 01:15:18.040
Tell him I'm mad at Jim because he's asking us to give money to Pam.
告诉他我生吉姆的气，因为他要求我们给帕姆捐钱。

1560
01:15:18.560 --> 01:15:20.460
This is Stanley Hudson.
这是斯坦利·哈德森。

1561
01:15:21.380 --> 01:15:23.720
Jim Halpert is a menace.
吉姆·哈珀特是个麻烦精。

1562
01:15:24.120 --> 01:15:25.580
It's Toby Flenderson.
我是托比·弗兰德森。

1563
01:15:26.400 --> 01:15:29.300
Listen, things are getting really bad down here.
听着，楼下的情况真的很糟糕。

1564
01:15:30.460 --> 01:15:32.120
Those are so funny to me.
我觉得那些太搞笑了。

1565
01:15:32.920 --> 01:15:34.600
But Jenna, there was one more.
但是珍娜，还有一个。

1566
01:15:35.240 --> 01:15:36.020
There was?
是吗？

1567
01:15:36.280 --> 01:15:36.520
Yes.
是的。

1568
01:15:36.820 --> 01:15:39.920
It didn't make it in the final cut, but it's in deleted scenes.
它没能进入最终剪辑版，但在删减片段里。

1569
01:15:40.140 --> 01:15:43.720
It's a little R-rated, so maybe that's why it didn't make it.
内容有点少儿不宜，所以可能这就是它没能入选的原因。

1570
01:15:43.940 --> 01:15:47.640
Here is Dwight calling, pretending to be Meredith.
这是德怀特打来的电话，假装是梅雷迪思。

1571
01:15:48.480 --> 01:15:49.740
It's Meredith Palmer.
我是梅雷迪思·帕尔默。

1572
01:15:50.100 --> 01:15:53.240
Listen, kid, I'm going to be drunk as a skunk.
听着，孩子，我到时候会烂醉如泥。

1573
01:15:53.520 --> 01:15:56.100
And you don't know what to tell me about crotch injuries.
而你根本不知道该怎么跟我说胯部受伤的事。

1574
01:15:56.980 --> 01:15:59.340
But Jim Halpert is a f***ing prick.
但吉姆·哈珀特是个混蛋。

1575
01:16:01.400 --> 01:16:08.510
Wallace getting all of these messages.
华莱士收到了所有这些留言。

1576
01:16:09.410 --> 01:16:13.850
Yeah, Jim is definitely going to be hearing from David Wallace later.
没错，吉姆之后肯定会收到大卫·华莱士的问候。

1577
01:16:14.150 --> 01:16:18.650
But back at the school, Michael and Erin are leaving.
镜头回到学校，迈克尔和艾琳正准备离开。

1578
01:16:18.650 --> 01:16:19.950
They are disgraced.
他们颜面扫地。

1579
01:16:20.510 --> 01:16:26.170
But as they're leaving, one of the students runs out and just kind of confronts Michael.
但就在他们离开时，一个学生跑出来，直接质问迈克尔。

1580
01:16:26.450 --> 01:16:27.170
He's like, dude.
他说，老兄。

1581
01:16:27.550 --> 01:16:27.930
Yeah.
是啊。

1582
01:16:28.490 --> 01:16:30.550
This is, like, really messed up.
这真的太过分了。

1583
01:16:30.590 --> 01:16:33.050
And Michael just apologizes again.
迈克尔又道了一次歉。

1584
01:16:33.050 --> 01:16:34.970
And he says, you know what?
他说，你知道吗？

1585
01:16:35.050 --> 01:16:36.490
I'll pay for your books.
我会帮你付书本费。

1586
01:16:36.510 --> 01:16:37.850
It's the least I can do.
这是我唯一能做的了。

1587
01:16:38.050 --> 01:16:38.290
Yeah.
是啊。

1588
01:16:38.710 --> 01:16:41.410
And he's like, okay, well, books are like $1,000.
那学生说，好吧，书本费大概要一千美元。

1589
01:16:42.010 --> 01:16:42.890
I mean, that's a lot.
我是说，那可是一大笔钱。

1590
01:16:42.890 --> 01:16:45.890
And Michael's like, that's like, oh, $200 a year.
迈克尔说，那大概，噢，一年两百美元吧。

1591
01:16:46.190 --> 01:16:49.510
And the kid's like, it's $1,000 a year.
那孩子说，是一年一千美元。

1592
01:16:49.710 --> 01:16:51.990
So Michael writes a few checks for $1,000.
于是迈克尔开了几张一千美元的支票。

1593
01:16:52.270 --> 01:16:54.510
He says, please notify me before you cash these.
他说，请在兑现这些支票前通知我。

1594
01:16:54.510 --> 01:16:56.330
I have to move some money around.
我得先周转一下资金。

1595
01:16:57.270 --> 01:16:57.750
Yes.
是的。

1596
01:16:57.870 --> 01:17:01.810
And he has to hold them for, like, a couple of years, each one per year.
而且他得把这些支票留着，大概留个几年，每年兑现一张。

1597
01:17:02.230 --> 01:17:06.090
Well, listen, the actor who played the student is so good.
听着，饰演那个学生的演员演得太好了。

1598
01:17:06.090 --> 01:17:08.010
His name is Kwame Boateng.
他的名字叫夸梅·博阿滕。

1599
01:17:08.510 --> 01:17:12.090
He is part of a trio, an acting trio.
他是三人组的一员，一个演艺三人组。

1600
01:17:12.090 --> 01:17:14.670
His brothers, they're referred to as the K brothers.
他的兄弟们被称为K兄弟。

1601
01:17:15.410 --> 01:17:16.430
He's amazing.
他太棒了。

1602
01:17:16.650 --> 01:17:18.570
He did a bunch of films and television.
他拍过很多电影和电视剧。

1603
01:17:18.570 --> 01:17:23.690
But now he is actually the CEO of his own company called the Boateng Group.
但现在他实际上是自己公司“博阿滕集团”的首席执行官。

1604
01:17:24.050 --> 01:17:24.590
Yeah.
没错。

1605
01:17:25.230 --> 01:17:28.110
So he's kind of moving and shaking in the business world now.
所以他现在在商界也算是个风云人物了。

1606
01:17:28.550 --> 01:17:32.870
And we also had a fan catch in this scene from Matthew in Franklin, Indiana.
我们还收到了一位来自印第安纳州富兰克林的粉丝马修发来的抓包。

1607
01:17:33.130 --> 01:17:37.870
At 16 minutes, 48 seconds, you can see snow outside the school.
在16分48秒处，你可以看到学校外面有雪。

1608
01:17:38.010 --> 01:17:38.470
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1609
01:17:38.650 --> 01:17:39.270
Fakie snow.
假雪。

1610
01:17:39.630 --> 01:17:43.870
Well, that fakie snow was provided by our special effects technician, Mike Thompson.
嗯，那场假雪是由我们的特效技师迈克·汤普森提供的。

1611
01:17:44.530 --> 01:17:49.910
According to Randy Cordray, it was actually a warm and sunny day in Van Nuys, about 75 degrees.
据兰迪·科德雷说，范奈斯那天其实是个温暖晴朗的日子，气温大约75华氏度。

1612
01:17:50.270 --> 01:17:52.190
But we threw down some fakie snow.
但我们还是撒了一些假雪。

1613
01:17:52.570 --> 01:17:58.670
Back in Jim's office, he does get a very frustrated call from David Wallace.
回到吉姆的办公室，他确实接到了大卫·华莱士打来的一个非常沮丧的电话。

1614
01:17:59.030 --> 01:18:04.170
I think we need to point out at 18 minutes, 7 seconds, the Phoebe Snow is back.
我觉得我们需要指出，在18分07秒处，“菲比·斯诺”号火车画又回来了。

1615
01:18:04.870 --> 01:18:05.890
It is?
是吗？

1616
01:18:05.890 --> 01:18:08.490
The train painting is in Jim's office.
那幅火车画就在吉姆的办公室里。

1617
01:18:08.790 --> 01:18:09.990
The Phoebe Snow is back.
“菲比·斯诺”号回来了。

1618
01:18:10.170 --> 01:18:13.070
That is so weird that it was missing for one episode.
它消失了一集，这真是太奇怪了。

1619
01:18:13.070 --> 01:18:14.090
I don't know.
我不知道。

1620
01:18:14.330 --> 01:18:16.670
Or maybe it's just the way they angled the camera.
或者可能只是摄像机角度的问题。

1621
01:18:16.810 --> 01:18:18.650
Maybe you just couldn't see it and I thought it was missing.
也许只是你没看见，而我以为它不见了。

1622
01:18:19.270 --> 01:18:20.350
Well, it's back.
好吧，它回来了。

1623
01:18:20.510 --> 01:18:20.630
It's back.
它回来了。

1624
01:18:20.630 --> 01:18:21.850
And did it make your heart happy?
它让你感到开心吗？

1625
01:18:21.970 --> 01:18:22.710
It really did.
确实如此。

1626
01:18:22.970 --> 01:18:27.590
You know, lady, if you love trains, you should play this board game called Ticket to Ride.
你知道吗，女士，如果你喜欢火车，你应该玩一款叫《车票之旅》的桌游。

1627
01:18:27.790 --> 01:18:28.830
I love Ticket to Ride.
我喜欢《车票之旅》。

1628
01:18:28.990 --> 01:18:30.110
I know Ticket to Ride.
我知道《车票之旅》。

1629
01:18:30.250 --> 01:18:32.110
Oh, we just discovered Ticket to Ride.
哦，我们刚发现《车票之旅》这款游戏。

1630
01:18:32.110 --> 01:18:34.590
Our friends sent it to us and now my kids are obsessed.
我们的朋友送给我们的，现在我的孩子们都着迷了。

1631
01:18:34.910 --> 01:18:35.170
Yeah.
是啊。

1632
01:18:35.550 --> 01:18:37.330
You've known about Ticket to Ride all this time?
你一直都知道《车票之旅》吗？

1633
01:18:37.470 --> 01:18:38.730
I was going to gift it to you.
我本来打算把它作为礼物送给你的。

1634
01:18:38.830 --> 01:18:39.950
I'm glad you told me you have it.
很高兴你告诉我你们已经有了。

1635
01:18:40.090 --> 01:18:41.170
Oh, yeah.
哦，是啊。

1636
01:18:41.930 --> 01:18:42.290
Okay.
好的。

1637
01:18:42.490 --> 01:18:43.850
We love games at my house.
我们家很喜欢玩游戏。

1638
01:18:43.910 --> 01:18:45.350
You know, we're big family game night, folks.
你知道的，我们家经常举办家庭游戏之夜。

1639
01:18:45.370 --> 01:18:48.610
Well, this was combining two of your loves, trains and a game.
嗯，这结合了你的两大爱好：火车和游戏。

1640
01:18:48.610 --> 01:18:52.990
We also really love the Oregon Trail, old school board game version, not the computer version
我们还非常喜欢《俄勒冈之旅》，是老派桌游版本，不是我们小时候玩的那种电脑版本。

1641
01:18:52.990 --> 01:18:53.690
we grew up on.
我们从小玩到大的那种。

1642
01:18:53.930 --> 01:18:58.870
Now, according to your deep dive last week, would a covered wagon be considered a limousine?
那么，根据你上周的深度挖掘，篷车会被视为豪华轿车吗？

1643
01:18:59.570 --> 01:19:01.110
Separation of driver and...
司机与……的分隔？

1644
01:19:01.110 --> 01:19:02.510
Because the driver is separated from the...
因为司机与……是隔开的。

1645
01:19:02.510 --> 01:19:02.990
Cargo?
货物？

1646
01:19:03.230 --> 01:19:03.510
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1647
01:19:04.030 --> 01:19:06.330
I think a completely covered wagon would be, yes.
我觉得完全封闭的篷车应该算，是的。

1648
01:19:06.890 --> 01:19:08.870
What part of the covered wagon is uncovered?
篷车的哪一部分是没遮盖的？

1649
01:19:09.070 --> 01:19:10.090
A little hole in the back?
后面有个小洞？

1650
01:19:10.090 --> 01:19:11.990
Sometimes they have a front flap that they keep open.
有时他们会留一个前帘敞开着。

1651
01:19:12.550 --> 01:19:14.250
But, I mean, same in a limousine.
但我的意思是，豪华轿车里也是一样的。

1652
01:19:14.430 --> 01:19:16.350
The little zhzzy thing goes down and up.
那个小隔板升上又降下。

1653
01:19:16.470 --> 01:19:17.130
No, I agree.
不，我同意。

1654
01:19:17.130 --> 01:19:18.550
I am agreeing.
我表示赞同。

1655
01:19:18.730 --> 01:19:19.950
This is me agreeing with you.
这就是我在表示赞同你。

1656
01:19:20.170 --> 01:19:25.990
I think a completely covered wagon with a driver outside would constitute as a limousine.
我觉得那种全封闭式、司机坐在外面的马车也算是一种豪华轿车。

1657
01:19:26.250 --> 01:19:26.730
Wow.
哇。

1658
01:19:27.550 --> 01:19:28.030
Limousine.
豪华轿车。

1659
01:19:28.750 --> 01:19:33.730
Tell, like, the early pioneers that they were actually taking limousines to the gold rush.
去告诉那些早期的拓荒者，说他们其实是坐着豪华轿车去淘金的。

1660
01:19:33.890 --> 01:19:35.730
They might be surprised.
他们可能会很惊讶。

1661
01:19:37.130 --> 01:19:39.490
Back to this phone call between Jim and David.
回到吉姆和戴维的那通电话上。

1662
01:19:39.990 --> 01:19:42.710
Dwight kind of overhears that it's not going well, right?
德怀特隐约听到进展不顺，对吧？

1663
01:19:42.870 --> 01:19:43.830
He's all excited.
他兴奋极了。

1664
01:19:43.970 --> 01:19:44.570
He's so excited.
他太兴奋了。

1665
01:19:44.670 --> 01:19:45.810
Jim's like, I don't know how it happened.
吉姆说，我不知道是怎么回事。

1666
01:19:45.810 --> 01:19:47.350
And Dwight's like, I know how it happened.
德怀特说，我知道是怎么回事。

1667
01:19:48.050 --> 01:19:52.550
Dwight goes back in there doing his little mom detective, drops a folder, grabs his spy
德怀特回去像个侦探老妈一样，掉落一个文件夹，抓住了他那枚

1668
01:19:52.550 --> 01:19:54.550
pin that's been in there the whole time.
一直都在那里的窃听器。

1669
01:19:54.750 --> 01:20:01.430
As it turns out, this phone call that starts out angry ends amicably.
事实证明，这通起初充满火药味的电话最后以和解告终。

1670
01:20:02.170 --> 01:20:02.970
David apologizes.
戴维道歉了。

1671
01:20:03.110 --> 01:20:05.150
He's like, look, I'm taking out some stuff on you, okay?
他说，听着，我把情绪发泄在你身上了，好吗？

1672
01:20:05.150 --> 01:20:06.330
Hey, am I going to see you at dinner?
嘿，晚餐时我能见到你吗？

1673
01:20:06.470 --> 01:20:07.490
And Dwight's like, no!
德怀特说，不行！

1674
01:20:07.490 --> 01:20:09.250
I know, he forgot.
我知道，他忘了。

1675
01:20:09.790 --> 01:20:12.090
Jim and David Wallace are chuMs.
吉姆和戴维·华莱士是好哥们。

1676
01:20:12.290 --> 01:20:12.870
They're pals.
他们是朋友。

1677
01:20:13.210 --> 01:20:17.650
The final scene with Michael and Erin, they're driving back.
迈克尔和艾琳的最后一幕，他们正在开车回去。

1678
01:20:18.010 --> 01:20:20.210
Erin can't stop singing the song.
艾琳不停地唱着那首歌。

1679
01:20:20.570 --> 01:20:20.910
Yeah.
是啊。

1680
01:20:20.910 --> 01:20:27.470
But then she says, you know, Michael, the principal told me that 90% of Scott's tots are on track
但随后她说，你知道吗，迈克尔，校长告诉我，90%的“斯科特小宝贝”都有望

1681
01:20:27.470 --> 01:20:31.330
to graduate, which is 35% higher than the rest of the school.
顺利毕业，这比学校其他学生高出35%。

1682
01:20:31.550 --> 01:20:34.530
So, you know, you did do a good thing here.
所以，你知道，你确实做了一件好事。

1683
01:20:35.150 --> 01:20:36.430
This warms Michael's heart.
这温暖了迈克尔的心。

1684
01:20:36.630 --> 01:20:39.370
He hasn't always been that nice to Erin.
他并不总是对艾琳那么好。

1685
01:20:39.650 --> 01:20:40.990
He's kind of abrupt with her.
他对她有点生硬。

1686
01:20:41.210 --> 01:20:44.330
She's not Pam, which he lets her know routinely.
她不是帕姆，他经常让她意识到这一点。

1687
01:20:45.110 --> 01:20:47.730
And he says to her, you know what?
然后他对她说，你知道吗？

1688
01:20:47.830 --> 01:20:48.590
You're doing great.
你做得很好。

1689
01:20:48.810 --> 01:20:51.310
And he wants to know, what does she hope for?
他想知道，她有什么愿望？

1690
01:20:51.750 --> 01:20:52.110
Yeah.
是啊。

1691
01:20:52.270 --> 01:20:54.030
What would she like for her future?
她对未来有什么期待？

1692
01:20:54.290 --> 01:20:58.050
She says she would like to be an accountant, even though she's terrible at math.
她说她想成为一名会计，尽管她数学很差。

1693
01:20:58.210 --> 01:21:03.030
I will tell you, this is a great nod to the webisode series, The Mentor, where Erin
我得告诉你，这是对网络剧《导师》的一个很棒的致敬，在那部剧里艾琳

1694
01:21:03.030 --> 01:21:05.950
tells the accounting department she wants to be an accountant.
告诉会计部门她想成为一名会计。

1695
01:21:06.170 --> 01:21:09.790
We talked about it last week, and I totally clocked it when she said that.
我们上周谈过这个，当她说出那句话时，我立刻就反应过来了。

1696
01:21:10.030 --> 01:21:16.970
We also learned something about Kevin's story in this moment, which is he was applying for
我们也在这一刻了解到了关于凯文故事的一些信息，那就是他当时正在申请

1697
01:21:16.970 --> 01:21:18.330
a job in the warehouse.
仓库的一份工作。

1698
01:21:18.910 --> 01:21:21.170
And Michael said, you know what?
迈克尔说，你知道吗？

1699
01:21:21.190 --> 01:21:22.290
I have a feeling about you.
我对你有种预感。

1700
01:21:22.570 --> 01:21:24.650
I think you should be an accountant.
我觉得你应该当会计。

1701
01:21:25.650 --> 01:21:25.990
Ah.
啊。

1702
01:21:26.870 --> 01:21:28.910
Well, this episode ends with a tag.
嗯，这一集结尾有个彩蛋。

1703
01:21:29.270 --> 01:21:31.950
All of a sudden, Ryan appears in this episode.
瑞安突然出现在这一集里。

1704
01:21:32.530 --> 01:21:35.570
And he finds Dwight's diabolical plan.
他发现了德怀特的邪恶计划。

1705
01:21:35.970 --> 01:21:36.090
Yeah.
没错。

1706
01:21:36.250 --> 01:21:37.490
Dwight left it in the copier.
德怀特把它落在了复印机里。

1707
01:21:37.770 --> 01:21:38.730
He wants in.
他想加入。

1708
01:21:38.830 --> 01:21:40.070
He wants to take Jim down.
他想搞垮吉姆。

1709
01:21:40.570 --> 01:21:41.010
Ooh.
噢。

1710
01:21:41.630 --> 01:21:43.530
That's how this episode ends.
这一集就是这样结束的。

1711
01:21:45.250 --> 01:21:48.670
Well, I had a couple little tidbits that I thought I would share.
嗯，我还有几个小花絮想和大家分享。

1712
01:21:48.770 --> 01:21:51.510
I didn't know where to put these, so I'm putting them here at the end.
我不知道该把它们放在哪儿，所以就放在最后了。

1713
01:21:51.930 --> 01:21:55.390
The first was a piece of mail we got from Julia S.
第一个是来自威斯康星州麦迪逊市的朱莉娅·S寄给我们的一封信。

1714
01:21:55.490 --> 01:21:56.770
in Madison, Wisconsin.
这事儿真让人尴尬。

1715
01:21:57.770 --> 01:21:58.810
This is cringy.
她说，我在一家非营利机构工作，我们曾有一个项目，结果成了“斯科特的学童”的翻版。

1716
01:21:58.810 --> 01:22:05.610
She said, I work at a nonprofit company, and we had a program that ended up being a
噢，不。

1717
01:22:05.610 --> 01:22:07.610
Scots Tots reincarnate.
她说这个项目的目标是鼓励小学生家长开始

1718
01:22:07.730 --> 01:22:08.390
Oh, no.
每月存一小笔钱，作为孩子未来的大学

1719
01:22:08.730 --> 01:22:13.810
She said the goal of the program was to encourage parents of elementary school kids to begin
学费。

1720
01:22:13.810 --> 01:22:18.450
putting away a small amount of money every month that would go toward their kids' college
她说，我们公司承诺，如果家长们这样做，公司会在孩子们上大学时提供一笔巨额奖学金。

1721
01:22:18.450 --> 01:22:19.030
tuitions.
但几年后，公司觉得要给所有孩子支付奖学金的承诺太沉重了。

1722
01:22:19.030 --> 01:22:25.550
She said, my company promised that if they did that, the company would give a huge scholarship
于是项目组不得不发邮件通知大家，奖学金计划取消了。

1723
01:22:25.550 --> 01:22:28.010
to each child when they began college.
天哪。

1724
01:22:28.170 --> 01:22:34.970
But after a couple of years, the company decided it was too big of a promise to pay scholarships
她说，现在我和同事们每次提到这个失败的项目都会感到尴尬，

1725
01:22:34.970 --> 01:22:36.210
to all the kids.
当我们谈起它时，我们管它叫“斯科特的学童”。

1726
01:22:36.210 --> 01:22:42.110
And the program had to send out an email to let everyone know that the scholarships weren't
呃。

1727
01:22:42.110 --> 01:22:42.710
going to happen.
但我不能以这种基调结束。

1728
01:22:43.050 --> 01:22:44.250
Oh, my gosh.
所以我给你们讲一个真实的感人故事，叫“戴尔的孩子们”。

1729
01:22:44.510 --> 01:22:49.930
She said, me and my colleagues now cringe every time someone mentions this failed program,
我想听听关于“戴尔的孩子们”的故事。

1730
01:22:49.930 --> 01:22:53.310
and when we talk about it, we call it Scots Tots.
当地报纸形容戴尔·施罗德是一个朴实的人，他出身贫寒，没上过大学，终身未婚，在同一家公司做了67年的木匠。

1731
01:22:53.970 --> 01:22:54.510
Ugh.
他们说他只有一条干活穿的牛仔裤，一条去教堂穿的牛仔裤，还有一辆雪佛兰卡车。

1732
01:22:54.970 --> 01:22:57.790
But I can't leave us on that note.
2005年他去世时，没有留下任何后代，但经过近70年的

1733
01:22:57.790 --> 01:23:03.050
So I wanted to leave you with this real-life story called Dale's Kids.
木工生涯和节俭生活，他攒下了近300万美元。

1734
01:23:03.370 --> 01:23:05.170
I want to hear about Dale's Kids.
这笔钱大部分进入了一个奖学金基金，帮助了33个人免费上了大学。

1735
01:23:05.390 --> 01:23:13.250
Dale Schroeder was described in his local paper as a simple man who grew up poor, never went
最近，这些受益于奖学金的孩子们聚在一起，谈论了这份奖学金对他们人生的影响。

1736
01:23:13.250 --> 01:23:19.330
to college, never got married, and worked at the same business as a carpenter for 67 years.
他们现在有的成了医生，有的成了老师，还有治疗师。

1737
01:23:19.610 --> 01:23:24.730
They said he had a pair of work jeans, a pair of church jeans, and a Chevy truck.
他们说，这笔钱只有一个附加条件。

1738
01:23:24.730 --> 01:23:31.790
When he passed away in 2005, he did not have any descendants, but after nearly 70 years of
他的要求是：请把这份爱传递下去。

1739
01:23:31.790 --> 01:23:35.310
carpentry and frugal living, he had saved nearly $3 million.
噢。

1740
01:23:36.450 --> 01:23:43.210
Most of that money went into a scholarship fund, which helped 33 people go to college free of
你无法报答戴尔，但你可以铭记他并效仿他。

1741
01:23:43.210 --> 01:23:43.710
charge.
这就是戴尔·施罗德留下的遗产，他们亲切地称自己为“戴尔的孩子们”。

1742
01:23:43.970 --> 01:23:49.550
The kids who benefited from this scholarship all gathered recently to talk about the impact
噢，那真是太美好了。

1743
01:23:49.550 --> 01:23:51.610
that the scholarship had on their lives.
她说道，我工作的非营利机构曾有一个项目，结果成了“斯科特的学童”的翻版。

1744
01:23:51.610 --> 01:23:54.610
They are now doctors, teachers, a therapiSt.
她说这个项目的目标是鼓励小学生家长开始

1745
01:23:55.090 --> 01:23:57.990
They said that the money came with only one caveat.
每月存一小笔钱，作为孩子未来的大学

1746
01:23:58.670 --> 01:24:01.850
Their request was, please pay this forward.
学费。

1747
01:24:02.230 --> 01:24:02.830
Aww.
她说，我们公司承诺，如果家长们这样做，公司会在孩子们上大学时提供一笔巨额奖学金。

1748
01:24:03.070 --> 01:24:06.810
You can't pay Dale back, but you can remember him and emulate him.
但几年后，公司觉得要给所有孩子支付奖学金的承诺太沉重了。

1749
01:24:07.330 --> 01:24:13.350
And that is the legacy of Dale Schroeder, and they affectionately call themselves Dale's Kids.
于是项目组不得不发邮件通知大家，奖学金计划取消了。

1750
01:24:13.350 --> 01:24:15.650
Oh, that is so lovely.
天哪。

1751
01:24:16.630 --> 01:24:18.550
Oh, Jenna, that is wonderful.
噢，珍娜，那真是太棒了。

1752
01:24:18.790 --> 01:24:22.990
Well, I had a quote to end this episode on, and now I feel bad saying it because that's
嗯，我本来准备了一句名言来结束这一集，但现在我不好意思说了，因为那句

1753
01:24:22.990 --> 01:24:24.510
such a nice sentiment to end on.
作为结尾的感言实在太美好了。

1754
01:24:24.750 --> 01:24:26.790
Well, I still want to hear your quote, lady.
没关系，我还是想听听你的名言，女士。

1755
01:24:27.390 --> 01:24:28.010
All right.
好吧。

1756
01:24:28.550 --> 01:24:30.930
This is from CheatSheet.com.
这段话来自 CheatSheet.com。

1757
01:24:31.210 --> 01:24:31.730
All right.
好吧。

1758
01:24:31.870 --> 01:24:33.870
We're taking a pivot here, folks.
各位，我们要转换一下话题了。

1759
01:24:35.170 --> 01:24:37.050
This is about this episode.
这是关于这一集的。

1760
01:24:37.050 --> 01:24:43.890
And I quote, if you're the kind of person who would like watching a taxidermist, or perhaps
引用如下：如果你是那种喜欢看动物标本剥制师工作，或者或许

1761
01:24:43.890 --> 01:24:50.030
would enjoy watching someone removing a splinter from the hand of a small child, then this episode
喜欢看别人帮小孩挑出手指里的刺的人，那么这一集

1762
01:24:50.030 --> 01:24:51.110
is for you.
就很适合你。

1763
01:24:51.330 --> 01:24:52.470
Well, that's perfect.
嗯，这评价太贴切了。

1764
01:24:52.690 --> 01:24:54.790
That is Scott's Tots.
这就是《斯科特的托儿们》那一集。

1765
01:24:54.850 --> 01:24:58.890
Of course, we owe a huge thank you to BJ Novak for being on the show today.
当然，我们非常感谢 B.J. 诺瓦克今天能来参加节目。

1766
01:24:58.890 --> 01:25:05.650
And thank you to Gene Stupnitsky, Lee Eisenberg, Paul Lieberstein, and Randy Cordray, and also to
还要感谢吉恩·斯图普尼茨基、李·艾森伯格、保罗·李伯斯汀和兰迪·科德雷，以及

1767
01:25:05.650 --> 01:25:08.290
James Carey, who helped me go through some digital clutter.
詹姆斯·凯里，他帮我清理了一些数字杂物。

1768
01:25:08.570 --> 01:25:14.190
Yes, and Joya Balfour for meeting me for coffee and bringing a trunk full of bobbleheads to me,
是的，还有乔亚·巴尔福，她和我喝咖啡，还给我带来了一后备箱的摇头娃娃，

1769
01:25:14.250 --> 01:25:17.690
and always sharing with us about what NBC.com was doing.
并总是与我们分享 NBC.com 的动态。

1770
01:25:17.870 --> 01:25:19.990
And thank you all for sending in your questions.
也感谢大家寄来的问题。

1771
01:25:20.350 --> 01:25:20.890
We love you.
我们爱你们。

1772
01:25:20.990 --> 01:25:21.790
We'll see you next week.
我们下周见。

1773
01:25:21.890 --> 01:25:22.510
Love you guys.
爱你们。

1774
01:25:23.010 --> 01:25:29.610
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1775
